[36mQuestion: Give a proof for the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality.[0m
[32mAnswer #1: Consider two vectors u and v in an inner product space.  For any scalar t, we have:

0 ≤ ||u + tv||² = ⟨u + tv, u + tv⟩ = ⟨u, u⟩ + 2t⟨u, v⟩ + t²⟨v, v⟩ = ||u||² + 2t⟨u, v⟩ + t²||v||²

This is a quadratic in t. Since it is non-negative, its discriminant must be non-positive:

(2⟨u, v⟩)² - 4||u||²||v||² ≤ 0

4⟨u, v⟩² ≤ 4||u||²||v||²

⟨u, v⟩² ≤ ||u||²||v||²

Taking the square root of both sides (and recognizing that norms are non-negative) gives the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality:

|⟨u, v⟩| ≤ ||u|| ||v||[0m
