[36mQuestion: Provide a proof for the Pythagorean theorem.[0m
[32mAnswer #2: Consider a right-angled triangle with legs a and b, and hypotenuse c.  Construct a square with side length a+b. Within this square, arrange four copies of the triangle to surround a smaller square with side length c. The area of the larger square is (a+b)².  The area of the four triangles is 4(1/2)ab = 2ab. The area of the inner square is c². Thus, (a+b)² = 2ab + c². Expanding, a² + 2ab + b² = 2ab + c². Subtracting 2ab from both sides yields a² + b² = c².[0m
