[Model Mapping] openai/o3 -> openai/o3-mini:high
Using openai/o3 with temperature 0.7
[36mQuestion: Give me a proof to Euclid's theorem of the infinitude of primes.[0m
[32mAnswer #2: Assume by contradiction that there are only finitely many primes. Let P be the product of all these primes. Now, consider the number N = P! + 1 (where P! is the factorial of P, meaning the product of all integers from 1 to P). Notice that every prime from our finite list divides P! exactly. However, when we divide N by any such prime, the factorial term gives a remainder of 0 while the added 1 gives a remainder of 1, implying no prime in our list divides N. Therefore, either N is itself prime or it has a prime factor not in our list. In either case, we obtain a contradiction, proving that there must be infinitely many primes.[0m
[35mCoherence Score: 90[0m
